    q1: ['Why is Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) so popular for combining BM25 and Vector Search?', 'BM25 scores (unbounded) and cosine similarities (`[-1, 1]`) are on completely different scales; RRF depends only on integer ranks (`1 / (k + rank)`), making fusion robust without brittle score-normalization tuning.'],
